int bc_debug_continue(bc_client_t *c);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Resumes command execution after the debugger has stopped at a
breakpoint.
The function sends a \f[CR]continue\f[R] command on
\f[CR]CHAN_DEBUG\f[R] (channel 4), which tells the server to exit the
break state and resume normal execution.
.PP
After continuing, execution proceeds until the next breakpoint is hit,
or until the command completes.
The debugger enters \f[CR]\(dqrun\(dq\f[R] mode.
.PP
This function is typically called from within a
\f[CR]bc_break_hit_cb\f[R] callback registered via
\f[CR]bc_debug_on_break_hit()\f[R], or after returning from the callback
while still in a \f[CR]bc_poll()\f[R] loop.
.PP
Calling \f[CR]bc_debug_continue()\f[R] when the debugger is not stopped
at a breakpoint is a no\-op and returns \f[CR]BC_OK\f[R].
